module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.concession_annotation_is_not_a_disposition

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data concession_annotation_is_not_a_disposition: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "concession_annotation_is_not_a_disposition" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a sentence that admits an invalid construction is allowed to stand in for deleting it** (INVALID STATE: an author identifies a decoration -- a fold that ignores its argument, a published column that is identically one arm for every row, or a located cause computed and then discarded -- and writes an annotation conceding that fact while leaving the construction in the executing surface. The concession is treated as the disposition.",

    "HARM, AND IT IS WORSE THAN NOT NOTICING.",

    "A missed decoration is a gap. A conceded decoration is a gap wearing diligence: the rule is stated, the author is visibly honest, and a reviewer who would have demanded deletion stops, because the sentence already did the work of noticing.",

    "The invalid state stays writable, a fold still reads it, and the next reader cites the concession as evidence the class is governed.",

    "DESIGN section 4c is why the costume works: no Accepted program can read the annotation, so the only thing that moved is what a human sees.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. It is not [[stale_present_tense_coverage_claim_in_the_authority_consulted_first]] -- that class ASSERTS COVERAGE that is false; this one ADMITS THE DEFECT and still ships the construction.",

    "It is not [[self_authorized_dissolution]] -- that class offers a trigger as PERMISSION to create debt; here the debt is already identified as something the module's own deletion rule would remove, and the annotation is offered as having removed it.",

    "It is not [[a_written_row_is_not_a_firing_mechanism]] -- that class files a ledger row and counts the filing as the remedy; here the missing act is a DELETION of a construction the author already classified, and no new row is required for the classification to have been correct.",

    "It is not an unmarked workaround: the defect is marked, which is exactly what conceals it.",

    "THE TELL is mechanical: the same change, or the same module header, both STATES a deletion rule and RETAINS a construction that rule would delete.",

    "SPECIMEN ONE, and it is the one this class was filed from.",

    "gunbc#10942's census derived every other column, then kept `RouteReach` / `reached_by_native_route` after gunbc#11003 deleted the required-v2-native lane.",

    "The axis had gone constant: `route_reach_of` ignored its argument, `ReachedByNativeRoute` had no constructor anywhere in the tree, and `census_counts` published `reached_by_native_route=` as a permanently-zero column -- DESIGN section 4b's decoration and DESIGN section 3c's dangling declaration.",

    "The previous cut KEPT THE AXIS and wrote an annotation conceding it had gone constant.",

    "The same module had just deleted the unread-verdict premise on exactly those grounds.",

    "Stating the rule and then not applying it is the class: the concession read as diligence while the decoration stayed, and a fold still published it.",

    "Review 63691 named it; the axis was deleted in `9142f62`.",

    "The author's own reply recorded that it was the third time in that PR a sentence acknowledging a problem was allowed to stand in for fixing it.",

    "SPECIMEN TWO, prior and already repaired, which is what establishes this as recurring rather than singular.",

    "`gunbc.package_delivery` `observe_protocol_schema_identity` computed a located cause and discarded it behind `ContentHash?`, while the annotation at that site said the cause \"reaches this line\" and that the next repair was to stop discarding it.",

    "Review 55992 on gunbc#9241 pointed out that registering a future repair is not a disposition: the distinction was computed and thrown away in the same change that computed it.",

    "The repair was to return `ProtocolSchemaIdentityObservation` so the cause reaches the caller in the type, not in the comment.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable.",

    "Both specimens survived until a reviewer joined the concession to the construction it left standing.",

    "CEILING AND NEXT TRIGGER, STATED PER SUB-CASE, BECAUSE A PLURAL LOSS WITH A SINGULAR TRIGGER IS THE GRAIN MISMATCH DESIGN section 4b(3) NAMES.",

    "THE ANNOTATION ITSELF CARRIES NO RUNG: whether a free-prose sentence is offered as a disposition rather than a description is not a property the source decides, so DESIGN section 4c puts that form in the adjacent column -- outside the modeled guarantee -- rather than at a low rung.",

    "SUB-CASE ONE, specimen one, ceiling mechanically preventable: a closed-roster producer that ignores its subject, or an axis identically fixed across the closed population.",

    "NEXT TRIGGER FOR SUB-CASE ONE: ingestion refuses a producer that ignores its subject, or an axis identically fixed across the closed population, rather than leaving that decoration describable beside the column.",

    "SUB-CASE TWO, specimen two, ceiling mechanically preventable: a located observation or cause is computed and then erased before it reaches the caller.",

    "NEXT TRIGGER FOR SUB-CASE TWO: the located observation or cause must remain in the returned carrier to the caller; a projection that computes then erases it is refused or unwritable. `ProtocolSchemaIdentityObservation` is the repaired exemplar, not the trigger.",

    "A constructor with no remaining inhabitant is not a third sub-case here: it has no measured owned trigger in this row, so it is not enumerated as a climb of this class. In specimen one it is a symptom of the axis having gone constant, owned by sub-case one, not a separate loss.",

    "NONE OF THOSE CAPABILITIES RETIRES THE GENERAL CONCESSION CLASS. Sub-case one can make a constant census column unwritable; sub-case two can make a discarded cause unwritable; neither decides whether an annotation is being offered as the disposition, which stays outside the modeled guarantee.",

    "A grep for \"gone constant\" / \"next repair\" / \"for now\" fires neither structured trigger; those phrases are how the concession is currently spelled, not the invalid state.)",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.v2_compile_obligation_census", decl_name: "census_counts"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.v2_compile_obligation_census", decl_name: "native_standing"),
    decl_ref(
      module_path: "gunbc.rung_drop.v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path",
      decl_name: "v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path"
    ),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.package_delivery", decl_name: "observe_protocol_schema_identity"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.package_delivery", decl_name: "ProtocolSchemaIdentityObservation"),
  ],
}
